WEBVTT

00:12.970 --> 00:18.710
Hikari ga sasu sora, umareochiru kage
In the bright sky illuminated by
sunlight, darkened shadows are born.

00:18.810 --> 00:24.150
Unmei wa dokomademo hikisakareru
Fate itself is being torn apart.

00:25.190 --> 00:30.150
Donna toki mo kesshite akiramenainara
If you never give up, no matter what happens,

00:30.330 --> 00:37.560
mada tozasareteru tobira kanarazu hiraku
Even that locked door will open for you.

00:38.530 --> 00:43.990
Eien datte dakishimete, fuuin mo tokihanachi
Embrace eternity and release the seal.

00:44.070 --> 00:49.940
Mamorubekimono ga ima kokoni wa arukara
Because the ones you wish
to protect are right here.

00:49.940 --> 00:55.880
Namida mo gyutto dakishimete,
yasashisa de tsutsumikomi
Embrace their tears with kindness.

00:55.880 --> 01:01.560
Nagareru mizu no youni tsuyoku nare
Become strong like the formless water,

01:01.560 --> 01:07.550
omouyouni tsuyoku nare
Become as strong as you wish to be.

01:07.700 --> 01:13.170
Mou jibun ni obienaide
Stop being afraid of yourself.

01:13.170 --> 01:19.800
Sou mirai wo osorenaide
Do not fear the future.

01:33.990 --> 01:36.420
All right! I got in.

01:36.420 --> 01:38.150
Didn't even know I could do it.

01:40.260 --> 01:41.920
Hey, kid.

01:42.430 --> 01:44.020
C'mere.

01:46.840 --> 01:48.100
A water blade.

01:48.340 --> 01:51.460
This isn't because of that fox.

01:51.710 --> 01:55.940
Dammit, I have such bad luck.

01:56.410 --> 02:00.040
My skin's been drooping recently.

02:00.420 --> 02:04.180
Probably because I wreaked some
havoc in the neighboring lands...

02:04.720 --> 02:08.560
I was thinking of drinking your
blood with your water affinities...

02:08.560 --> 02:12.520
I'll get all the gleam and shine back on my skin.

02:12.830 --> 02:17.320
You have bad luck, y'know? With your
birth and the workings of your body.

02:19.270 --> 02:20.860
Damn, this is annoying.

02:21.400 --> 02:22.800
Yeah, I know. I know.

02:28.980 --> 02:33.940
Our Fox Deity, Embraces a Fox Cub

02:42.720 --> 02:43.710
Ko-chan.

02:44.030 --> 02:44.550
Yes?

02:44.860 --> 02:46.590
Did you help me today?

02:48.800 --> 02:50.290
I will always be here to protect you.

02:50.570 --> 02:52.830
Oh, okay. Thanks.

02:53.200 --> 02:54.070
My pleasure.

02:57.340 --> 02:59.740
Talisman made from the fur
of the Kugen Fox of Mizuchi!

03:03.180 --> 03:04.410
That's...

03:05.480 --> 03:07.680
You there. Hold on a second.

03:08.280 --> 03:09.310
I said wait!

03:11.950 --> 03:14.420
Oh, another fox.

03:14.720 --> 03:16.550
You still seem to be pretty young.

03:17.060 --> 03:18.490
Who the hell are you?!

03:18.760 --> 03:23.560
Just the god governing this area.

03:23.700 --> 03:26.060
You're the presiding god here?

03:26.430 --> 03:30.430
Yep. I'm Ebisu. Nice to meet ya.

03:30.840 --> 03:32.400
I-I'm terribly sorry!

03:33.370 --> 03:37.400
Sorry 'bout that. I didn't mean to trip you.

03:37.780 --> 03:39.550
So what brings you to this land?

03:39.550 --> 03:45.090
The mountain where I lived was
deforested by humans recently.

03:45.090 --> 03:46.850
I can't live there anymore.

03:47.990 --> 03:52.060
You hear about those things a lot around here.
You have my condolences.

03:52.060 --> 03:57.500
The other day, I felt the metal
aura of a fox from this land.

03:57.700 --> 04:05.000
It must be a very powerful fox,
so I came to ask for advice.

04:07.580 --> 04:11.100
The fox you're looking for is a tenko.
The Kugen Fox of the Mizuchi.

04:12.910 --> 04:15.380
That's an even bigger name than I thought.

04:15.680 --> 04:19.190
If you're really in trouble,
I'm sure that fox will help you out.

04:19.190 --> 04:20.620
Why not go and pay it a visit?

04:23.120 --> 04:24.890
And that's what he said...

04:25.230 --> 04:28.800
That Ebisu... What is he plotting this time?

04:28.800 --> 04:32.360
Oh, who cares? He has a small child with him.

04:32.570 --> 04:35.660
I doubt it's not all bad.

04:37.210 --> 04:40.880
Say. Why don't you take that hood off?
Aren't you hot?

04:40.880 --> 04:43.000
If you insist.

04:46.810 --> 04:48.210
I-It's...

04:51.120 --> 04:53.320
It's so cute!

04:53.320 --> 04:56.560
I want to hug him!

04:56.560 --> 05:00.160
I want to hug him, too.

05:00.160 --> 05:01.360
Squish, squish!

05:04.370 --> 05:05.860
Come over here.

05:15.240 --> 05:17.140
How adorable.

05:17.410 --> 05:18.710
What's his name?

05:20.110 --> 05:22.410
Neither of us have one yet.

05:23.520 --> 05:26.650
I see. Then I'll name him for you.

05:27.620 --> 05:29.060
Thank you!

05:29.290 --> 05:31.090
It would be wonderful to have
the tenko give him a name.

05:33.290 --> 05:36.630
How about Daigoro? Like in the book.

05:38.330 --> 05:42.330
So the dad is going to be Ogami Itto...

05:48.740 --> 05:49.970
I'm home.

05:54.920 --> 05:58.320
I-It's so cute! What is this?!

05:58.320 --> 06:00.220
Where'd you find it?!

06:00.220 --> 06:00.690
- Haruki, do you mind if they stay for a while?

06:00.690 --> 06:03.820
- There, there, there. Squishy squishy!
- Haruki, do you mind if they stay for a while?

06:04.160 --> 06:05.390
They're yokai, though.

06:05.660 --> 06:07.590
Sure, I don't mind! I don't mind at all!

06:07.860 --> 06:09.860
What're their names?

06:09.860 --> 06:11.530
It's so cute!

06:14.640 --> 06:16.900
What will happen to us?

06:28.250 --> 06:29.720
Don't... ask.

06:34.360 --> 06:40.360
Clams, soy sauce, tomatoes, wasabi and also...

06:40.360 --> 06:43.460
Hmm... Kudzu root medicine.

06:43.460 --> 06:44.670
No.

06:44.670 --> 06:46.000
Chopped seaweed.

06:47.240 --> 06:48.970
Why don't you write it down?

06:48.970 --> 06:51.400
That's all right. I can remember it.

06:51.540 --> 06:52.770
But...

06:52.770 --> 06:55.210
Noboru-san. Please let me go.

06:57.250 --> 07:00.040
But you're a guest at our house.

07:00.250 --> 07:03.740
You're doing so much for us,
so at least let me help with the shopping!

07:03.850 --> 07:04.880
Really?

07:05.020 --> 07:06.950
Then, if you don't mind...

07:06.950 --> 07:10.320
No. I'm the one ordered to do this. I will go.

07:10.320 --> 07:12.730
I can stay in human form, so it'll be okay.

07:12.730 --> 07:14.850
Oh, but...

07:17.570 --> 07:19.000
Why don't you go together?

07:23.170 --> 07:25.230
Let's see... Next, we need...

07:25.470 --> 07:26.630
Kudzu root medicine.

07:35.120 --> 07:37.110
I'm sure you felt hot in that, Daigoro.

07:38.790 --> 07:42.720
We can go take a bath together later,
Daigoro-chan.

07:46.160 --> 07:47.220
Um...

07:48.200 --> 07:53.730
Why are Tenko-sama's powers weaker than usual?

07:54.340 --> 07:56.000
It used the Spirit Passing spell.

08:00.910 --> 08:02.600
So that's why...

08:08.050 --> 08:08.910
What is it?

08:09.620 --> 08:11.210
I felt someone...

08:15.220 --> 08:17.160
What is this?!

08:18.590 --> 08:22.260
This fog... Is it cutting us off from the elements?

08:22.460 --> 08:26.230
Possibly. It may be to stop
us from casting any spells.

08:27.170 --> 08:28.470
Watch out!

08:29.100 --> 08:30.100
A-Are you okay?!

08:30.100 --> 08:33.230
This is... a water blade.

08:34.240 --> 08:38.050
Applying earth to water gives
rise to the metal affinity.

08:38.050 --> 08:41.780
Apply the wood affinity on
top of that to create a blade.

08:41.780 --> 08:46.810
And thus, a blade of water is created...

09:05.040 --> 09:07.440
He's a shelled yokai.

09:08.780 --> 09:10.410
Wasn't that water blade well-made?

09:10.410 --> 09:14.710
If you can do it, so can I, little girl.

09:16.220 --> 09:18.850
I don't understand.

09:18.850 --> 09:20.980
It's about what happened in that kid's dream.

09:21.290 --> 09:24.550
I'll get you back for what you did then, human.

09:25.160 --> 09:28.290
Kid? You mean Toru-sama?

09:28.660 --> 09:30.860
Who else would it be?

09:31.970 --> 09:35.330
What could that shelled yokai be after?

09:35.600 --> 09:38.090
He probably wants Toru-sama.

09:38.710 --> 09:41.080
And we are obstacles in his path.

09:41.080 --> 09:43.070
Toru-san? Why would he do that?

09:43.440 --> 09:47.470
Noboru-sama and Toru-sama are
direct descendants of the Mizuchi.

09:47.580 --> 09:50.810
Of the Mizuchi? I didn't know that!

09:54.560 --> 09:57.460
This is really hard to deal with.
Especially if the elements are cut off from us...

09:57.460 --> 09:59.930
Ogami-san, can you summon anything?

10:00.090 --> 10:04.670
I'm sorry. I tried to learn, but I can't.

10:04.670 --> 10:07.400
It's all right. I can't either.

10:07.540 --> 10:10.240
But that's because you're a human.

10:10.240 --> 10:12.870
But I am the Mamorime.

10:19.880 --> 10:21.710
You got a nice ass on you!

10:22.820 --> 10:24.940
The things Noboru-sama asked us to buy...

10:30.060 --> 10:31.120
Rinsenmon...

10:38.900 --> 10:40.660
It's no use.

10:41.570 --> 10:45.340
In this fog, you can't win...

10:49.710 --> 10:50.750
I-Impossible!

10:50.750 --> 10:53.310
There shouldn't be any water here...

10:53.310 --> 10:54.680
How did you use a spell?

10:58.320 --> 11:00.620
With soy sauce?!

11:01.060 --> 11:03.390
Toru-sama will never be yours.

11:03.690 --> 11:06.060
End this now unless you want to get hurt again.

11:08.060 --> 11:09.550
Never!

11:11.300 --> 11:13.130
H-Hey! Mamorime-san!

11:13.330 --> 11:15.300
Wait! H-Hey!

11:24.510 --> 11:27.110
Give up on chasing after Toru-sama.

11:28.020 --> 11:30.070
Neener neener neener!

11:39.760 --> 11:41.960
That's just a clone I made, stupid.

11:41.960 --> 11:44.450
How can you fall for something so simple?

11:46.330 --> 11:51.700
Rinsenmon. So you have a dragon in your body.

11:51.910 --> 11:54.030
That explains a lot...

11:55.180 --> 11:58.250
I get inconvenienced with you around.

11:58.250 --> 12:01.040
You mind if you died for me?

12:01.950 --> 12:03.140
The dragons...

12:03.820 --> 12:09.120
Have absolute mastery over water!

12:13.830 --> 12:15.390
Not bad at all.

12:15.700 --> 12:21.600
But I'm a yokai of the water affinity.
Water-based spells have no effect on me.

12:21.940 --> 12:27.170
Your water spells actually give me more power.

12:28.040 --> 12:31.600
Applying earth to water gives
rise to the metal affinity.

12:31.950 --> 12:36.910
Apply the wood affinity on
top of that to create a blade.

12:39.150 --> 12:42.210
What's this ringing in my ears?

12:43.290 --> 12:45.190
Nah, it's probably my imagination.

12:47.460 --> 12:53.230
And thus the blade of water is created...

12:57.470 --> 12:58.460
Mamorime-san!

12:58.870 --> 13:01.810
Are you okay?! Are you hurt?!

13:02.310 --> 13:05.400
I'm fine. Thank you.

13:06.550 --> 13:08.340
It's nothing...

13:09.750 --> 13:14.310
Having another worthless punk
added into the mix won't help you!

13:14.560 --> 13:16.050
The hell did you say?!

13:20.390 --> 13:22.990
Hey, shrine maiden.
You're with the dragons, aren't you?

13:23.200 --> 13:24.720
Go ahead! Try and fight back!

13:30.000 --> 13:32.200
You humans can't do anything.

13:32.510 --> 13:35.630
You managed to summon an element,
but that's the best you got...

13:41.520 --> 13:43.510
The hell?!

13:44.520 --> 13:46.580
What's going on with him?

13:47.120 --> 13:49.780
Why?! How?

13:50.160 --> 13:52.060
He has been poisoned by the water element.

13:53.130 --> 13:58.660
I've been directing the water element
into him ever since we entered the park.

13:59.030 --> 14:00.800
It was much easier to do than I thought.

14:01.240 --> 14:02.900
I don't really understand.

14:03.070 --> 14:05.770
The flooding of the water
element poisons the kidney.

14:05.770 --> 14:12.850
While the system of the kidney produces marrow
and feeds the brain, it also controls the Fire of Life.

14:12.850 --> 14:16.550
When its functions are halted, he'll be
plagued with dizziness and ringing in his ears.

14:16.550 --> 14:20.210
His appendages will grow weak,
making him unable to stand.

14:20.390 --> 14:25.920
But he's shelled. How would a water-elemental
yokai like him be poisoned by water?

14:26.290 --> 14:28.730
There is a limit to everything.

14:29.300 --> 14:32.660
Once he absorbs a little more water...

14:46.780 --> 14:49.080
So that's his original form...

14:50.350 --> 14:52.380
Oh, right! Clams, Ogami-san.

14:52.850 --> 14:54.650
We forgot to buy clams.

14:54.820 --> 14:58.220
That's right! I forgot, too.

15:02.900 --> 15:05.830
This obviously isn't edible.

15:05.830 --> 15:06.800
It's edible.

15:06.800 --> 15:08.770
I-I'm the kind you keep in aquariums!

15:08.770 --> 15:09.630
It talked.

15:09.840 --> 15:12.970
- Please give me a break! Please! Please!
- I still say you can eat it.

15:12.970 --> 15:14.910
- Please give me a break! Please! Please!
- Are you sure?

15:14.910 --> 15:19.110
- Oh yeah, I taste really bitter!
- I'm not sure I want to eat something that talks.

15:20.980 --> 15:22.750
You need to get some rest.

15:22.750 --> 15:26.380
All right. Daigoro-chan, come with me.

15:29.520 --> 15:30.660
Who could it be?

15:30.660 --> 15:32.160
Yes?

15:32.160 --> 15:33.750
Hello!

15:34.500 --> 15:35.520
Oh, the komainu guys.

15:35.960 --> 15:37.690
May we come in?

15:38.100 --> 15:39.570
Uhh, sure.

15:59.920 --> 16:02.820
Do you like baths, Daigoro-chan?

16:05.090 --> 16:07.580
Oh, is this the first time you took a bath?

16:17.440 --> 16:18.460
Well...

16:18.540 --> 16:21.840
We would like you to give us that clam.

16:21.840 --> 16:22.710
Why?

16:23.010 --> 16:29.150
Er, there's this presiding deity in the
neighboring area called Mubyo...

16:29.150 --> 16:30.180
Mubyo?

16:30.180 --> 16:31.490
You know who it is?

16:31.490 --> 16:33.290
Well...

16:33.290 --> 16:34.660
That god's famous.

16:34.660 --> 16:36.780
I've heard that god is really scary.

16:37.190 --> 16:40.090
Rumors say Mubyo is quick
to settle things with violence.

16:40.230 --> 16:45.200
That thing there incited the wrath of
Mubyo-sama and was expelled from the lands.

16:45.200 --> 16:47.900
That is why it took up
residence in this land recently.

16:48.040 --> 16:52.270
What did it do to incite the
wrath of a presiding god?

16:53.870 --> 16:56.070
It's not the Spirit Passing spell, is it?

16:57.640 --> 17:00.370
It is something about stealing
the Sakasaen or whatnot.

17:00.480 --> 17:02.120
The Sakasaen?

17:02.120 --> 17:03.740
What's that?

17:04.150 --> 17:09.210
A divine treasure that allows you to move
backwards in the flow of the Five Phases.

17:09.520 --> 17:11.680
So it was Mubyo who had it.

17:12.130 --> 17:20.670
After Mubyo-sama found out he was here,
that deity's wrath fell upon our master.

17:20.670 --> 17:24.170
Mubyo-sama said, "If the clam was
not captured alive and brought forth...

17:24.170 --> 17:27.370
...I'll skin you alive and sell the
scraps to a shamisen maker!"

17:27.570 --> 17:28.800
That's what we heard.

17:28.880 --> 17:30.100
Sounds scary...

17:30.380 --> 17:34.280
Why doesn't that Mubyo person
come to catch the clam personally?

17:34.280 --> 17:39.490
Presiding deities, as a general rule, cannot
intervene in the lands governed by other gods.

17:39.490 --> 17:42.110
Did Ebisu agree to handing the clam over?

17:42.460 --> 17:43.120
Yes.

17:43.120 --> 17:45.180
Not for free, I assume.

17:45.260 --> 17:50.360
Of course not! The one who catches the
clam will be bestowed land by Mubyo as a...

17:50.360 --> 17:51.660
Koga!

17:51.970 --> 17:52.660
Whoops...

17:53.070 --> 17:54.030
I knew it.

17:55.900 --> 17:59.460
So he's going to take the clam as if he caught it
and get the gift?! That's not fair!

17:59.670 --> 18:04.370
Wait, when you say bestowed,
that means he'll get the land?

18:04.580 --> 18:06.070
W-Well, yes.

18:06.680 --> 18:07.510
You are correct.

18:07.750 --> 18:10.820
Then we should be the ones to receive the reward.

18:10.820 --> 18:16.520
This involves a sort of spiritual formality so you
won't receive any sort of monetary benefit.

18:16.860 --> 18:20.920
As an ordinary human, it would
not be worth anything to you.

18:21.060 --> 18:25.050
It's not for me. I'm going to give it to Ogami-san.

18:25.370 --> 18:28.160
Ogami-san is looking for a place to live.

18:28.440 --> 18:32.100
Besides, it was Ogami-san who caught the clam.

18:35.040 --> 18:39.500
For someone who's always daydreaming,
you can be really sharp at times.

18:40.810 --> 18:42.120
Well, you heard him.

18:42.120 --> 18:45.310
We have no intention of giving you the clam.

18:45.690 --> 18:47.350
Go back and tell that to your master.

18:47.350 --> 18:48.520
No, but...

18:48.520 --> 18:49.510
Then we'll...

18:53.160 --> 18:53.850
What is this?

18:54.230 --> 18:55.560
How adorable!

18:55.830 --> 18:58.630
That's Ogami-san's son. He's called Daigoro-chan.

18:59.930 --> 19:01.460
Daigoro-chan, I see.

19:04.770 --> 19:09.440
Excuse me. Did Daigoro-chan come here?

19:10.240 --> 19:11.400
He's right over here.

19:12.710 --> 19:15.110
Daigoro-chan. Come over here.

19:16.580 --> 19:18.240
You need to be dried off.

19:21.460 --> 19:22.350
Daigoro-chan!

19:23.060 --> 19:23.920
There we go.

19:24.630 --> 19:28.230
You'll catch a cold if you don't dry off.
That goes for you too, Ko-chan.

19:28.230 --> 19:30.490
I know. Thank you for your concern.

19:31.060 --> 19:32.550
Now if you'll excuse me.

19:33.670 --> 19:36.440
That was a great sight to see.

19:36.440 --> 19:38.200
You got that right...

19:38.610 --> 19:40.540
You two saw it, didn't you?

19:41.510 --> 19:47.680
There is a traditional law that decrees any
who sees the bare legs of the Mamorime...

19:47.680 --> 19:50.410
...must give something valuable
in return to the family of Mizuchi.

19:50.620 --> 19:51.920
Wh-What is that?!

19:51.920 --> 19:53.150
You're talking crazy!

19:54.050 --> 19:54.920
- Is that true? When did that law start?

19:54.920 --> 19:56.090
- B-But it's an old law...
- Is that true? When did that law start?

19:56.090 --> 19:57.560
- But still...
- Is that true? When did that law start?

19:57.720 --> 19:58.590
Right now.

19:58.860 --> 20:01.020
I-It was an accident.

20:01.600 --> 20:04.030
I'm not asking for your life.

20:04.400 --> 20:07.230
Just leave the clam with us.

20:09.540 --> 20:10.160
Toru-san.

20:10.970 --> 20:13.540
Are you sure we should have that land?

20:13.540 --> 20:16.030
I don't mind. It's not like I want it.

20:16.380 --> 20:17.410
What about you, Tenko-sama?

20:17.410 --> 20:18.940
I'm not interested in land.

20:23.720 --> 20:25.290
Thank you very much.

20:25.290 --> 20:28.550
I will never forget this debt I have to you.

20:28.760 --> 20:30.090
Wait, no!

20:30.090 --> 20:32.320
We have duties we must fulfill!

20:32.590 --> 20:36.300
You guys came all the way
out here in the summer heat...

20:36.300 --> 20:38.070
Here, have this.

20:38.070 --> 20:40.070
Fried rice!

20:40.070 --> 20:41.690
It even has boiled pork in there, too!

20:41.940 --> 20:44.300
It's his special homemade pork!

20:44.810 --> 20:47.040
I had a lot of free time because
of summer vacation so I made it.

20:47.040 --> 20:48.970
Come on, help yourself.

20:49.110 --> 20:50.540
Time to eat!

20:51.380 --> 20:53.150
This is delicious.

20:53.150 --> 20:55.240
The current Mizuchi head is very good at cooking.

20:58.150 --> 20:59.120
You ate it.

21:00.390 --> 21:04.260
I never said anything about letting you eat for free.

21:05.390 --> 21:08.300
You're not going to dine-and-dash on me, are you?

21:08.300 --> 21:09.390
Are you?

21:09.730 --> 21:11.290
Of course they won't.

21:22.380 --> 21:28.800
Sora no hate ga tsunagaru basho wo
Where the horizon meets the earth,

21:29.320 --> 21:36.520
no ni saku hana wa mada kitto shiranai
The flower growing in the wild remains unaware.

21:37.860 --> 21:44.350
Kokoyori ii sekai ga aruto
While thinking that there
is a world better than this.

21:44.530 --> 21:52.170
